{"agent":"fx-cli-queue","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`every` defaults to `True`, so a bare direct call `bug_file_tasks(repo)` still computes `preview = not bug_id and not every` as `False`, leaves `dry_run` as `False`, and writes fix tasks for every open bug. This is the same accidental bulk-filing behavior the change is meant to make a preview, and it contradicts the function’s own docstring that “with neither a bug nor `every` this is a preview.” The default should be `every=False` (or the surfaces must never be able to call it without an explicit `every`).","digest":"d32d9af102205859","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:bug_file_tasks","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:bug_file_tasks"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `bug_id` existence/open check runs against the `st` returned by `_load` before entering `log.transaction()`, but the work inside the transaction re-reads `fold(log.read_all(), strict=False)`. In a concurrent ddflow interleaving, another agent can add or close bug `X` after this process calls `_load` but before it acquires the transaction lock. Then `bug_file_tasks(repo, bug_id=\"X\")` either returns `O.failed(\"no such bug 'X'\")` even though the ledger inside the transaction contains `X`, or later reports a now-closed bug as “already has a fix task” instead of failing as required. The check should be done on the reloaded `st` inside the transaction.","digest":"39931694faf7dd29","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:bug_file_tasks","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:bug_file_tasks"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":17057,"diff_sha":"9726de50ca9a1d9654e3b5c71136a825eb85e0690e0d4bd340a4c8859a3533a6","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":523.7,"excluded_bytes":477